          ],
          "content": "170"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.0,
            0.098,
            0.242,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.056,
                0.277,
                0.225,
                0.294
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 9.9: Decantation"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.084,
            0.636,
            0.104
          ],
          "content": "Dada: I shall prepare tea for you."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.104,
            0.626,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": "Children: We will also help you."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.125,
            0.882,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": "As Dada makes the tea, he shares tips on how to make a cup of tea."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.166,
            0.882,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "Balan: After preparing tea, how do you remove the tea leaves?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.206,
            0.883,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "Dada: Obviously, with a strainer. You know if we do not have a strainer, we can still remove most of the tea leaves."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.247,
            0.413,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "Valli: How?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.268,
            0.882,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "Dada: Leave the sauce pan (vessel) containing tea undisturbed for some time and gently pour the tea in a cup (Fig. 9.9)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.328,
            0.882,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "Valli: Oh Yes! And then the tea leaves will be settled at the bottom."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.39,
            0.225,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "Decantation is also used in washing and cleaning of rice and pulses."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.369,
            0.883,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "The process of settling down of heavier insoluble component at the bottom of a liquid is called **sedimentation**. When the water (liquid) is removed by tilting the vessel, the process is called **decantation**."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.03,
            0.494,
            0.251,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.498,
            0.343,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.369,
            0.478,
            0.856,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "In the chapter 'Materials Around Us', you have studied that oil does not mix with water and forms a separate laver when left undisturbed for some time. Which method of separation would you use to separate oil and water?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.623,
            0.883,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "Dada: But I can still get a few tea leaves in my mouth because decantation does not completely separate all the tea leaves from the tea."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.684,
            0.881,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "Balan: Oh! It means it is not a proper method of separation. Dada: Yes, you are right. The tea is ready now."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.724,
            0.882,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "Malli picks up the tea-strainer from the shelf and gives it to his Dada."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.765,
            0.882,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "Dada: Let me pour the tea through this strainer. You can see all the tea leaves collected in the strainer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.804,
            0.882,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": "This process of separating tea leaves from tea is called **filtration**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.844,
            0.882,
            0.884
          ],
          "content": "Balan asks Malli if he could use a tea strainer to filter muddy water. Let us try and find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.885,
            0.882,
            0.926
          ],
          "content": "Dada: Also, try to filter the muddy water through a piece of cloth and observe the difference."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
